# ==============================================================
# FILE: frontend/.env.development
# ==============================================================
# OWNER:        Team Member 1 (Frontend Developer)
# TECHNOLOGIES: Vite Environment Variables, Node.js/Express,
#               Flask/Python, Docker Compose Networking
#
# INSTRUCTIONS FOR TEAM MEMBER 1:
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file holds environment-specific configuration variables
# for the LOCAL DEVELOPMENT environment. Vite reads this file
# automatically when running `npm run dev`. All variables MUST
# be prefixed with VITE_ to be exposed to the browser bundle.
#
# STEPS TO IMPLEMENT:
#
# 1. Node.js Backend API Base URL:
#    - Set VITE_NODE_API_URL to the URL of the Express backend.
#    - In local development (without Docker), use:
#        VITE_NODE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
#    - When using Docker Compose, use the container service name:
#        VITE_NODE_API_URL=http://node-backend:5000
#      (Docker Compose DNS resolves service names automatically.)
#
# 2. Flask Analytics Backend URL:
#    - Set VITE_FLASK_API_URL to the URL of the Flask backend.
#    - In local development (without Docker), use:
#        VITE_FLASK_API_URL=http://localhost:5001
#    - When using Docker Compose, use:
#        VITE_FLASK_API_URL=http://flask-backend:5001
#
# 3. Application Metadata Variables:
#    - VITE_APP_NAME=PassCraft
#    - VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0
#    - VITE_APP_ENV=development
#
# 4. Feature Flags (optional):
#    - VITE_ENABLE_ANALYTICS=true
#    - VITE_ENABLE_TICKET_GENERATION=true
#
# 5. Usage in Code:
#    - Access in any React component or utility:
#        const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_NODE_API_URL;
#    - NEVER hardcode API URLs inside component files.
#    - Always use import.meta.env.VITE_* variables instead.
#
# 6. Important Security Rules:
#    - DO NOT put secrets, API keys, or passwords in this file.
#      This file is bundled INTO the browser JavaScript — it is
#      publicly visible to anyone who inspects the bundle.
#    - Secrets belong ONLY in backend .env files which are never
#      bundled or shipped to the client.
#    - This file IS committed to source control (unlike .env files
#      in the backend) because it contains no sensitive data.
#
# 7. Production Overrides:
#    - Create a separate .env.production file for production URLs.
#    - Vite will automatically use .env.production when running
#      `npm run build`.
# ==============================================================

VITE_NODE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
VITE_FLASK_API_URL=http://localhost:5001
VITE_APP_NAME=PassCraft
VITE_APP_VERSION=1.0.0
VITE_APP_ENV=development
